message: "If you use this proof or checker, cite this archive and the works listed in UPSTREAM.md."
title: "Twenty-one is the last uniquely shaped Walsh support cardinality"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yongxian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3864-3536"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
abstract: "Across ambient dimensions, Boolean functions with Walsh support of size 21 give one affine support shape. Every cardinality at least 22 admits at least two shapes. The proof uses an external published six-variable catalog for its finite base case, original finite witnesses, and uniform constructions for larger sizes. It answers the first open question in the April 2026 preprint of Jauberty and Méaux."
